Description: stack-overflow test: also accept a regex that rejects the pattern without recursing
 The test feeds grep up to 10 million "(" and expects either gnulib's c-stack
 "stack overflow" diagnostic or (for a regex that avoids deep recursion) exit
 status 1 with no output. A C library whose regcomp parses iteratively reports
 the pattern as what it is, "Unmatched ( or \(", with exit status 2, exactly as
 grep does for a handful of "(". Accept that too.
Author: Yohane Linux Maintainers <aqours@koiren.ai>
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/tests/stack-overflow
+++ b/tests/stack-overflow
@@ -50,4 +50,13 @@
   && ! test -s err \
   && Exit 0

+# Yohane: a regex that parses the pattern without deep recursion (libniji's)
+# rejects it the same way it rejects a few unmatched parentheses: exit status 2,
+# no output, and the usual diagnostic. That is a working regex too.
+test $st = 2 \
+  && ! test -s out \
+  && grep -q 'Unmatched ( or \\(' err \
+  && test "$(wc -l < err)" = 1 \
+  && Exit 0
+
 fail_ 'grep never printed "stack overflow"'
